105
00:07:39,201 --> 00:07:43,203
Both leaks need no tools and no access to the build machine:

106
00:07:43,203 --> 00:07:49,674
only the image, which is usually pushed to a registry that many people and systems can pull from.

107
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:52,996
Let me try something.

108
00:07:52,996 --> 00:07:55,823
"But the credentials file is deleted":

109
00:07:55,823 --> 00:07:59,468
the Dockerfile copies it, uses it and removes it.

110
00:08:00,033 --> 00:08:06,600
A container shows only the top of the layer stack; deleting a file in a later layer only hides it.

111
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:11,425
The layer that COPY created is still in the image, and every copy of it.

112
00:08:11,425 --> 00:08:14,843
Export the image and read the file from that layer:

113
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:21,020
