Read-only file system errors name the exact path that needs to be writable.

143
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:37,365
Can you show me linux capabilities?

144
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:42,825
Linux splits the power of root into about 40 capabilities:

145
00:10:42,825 --> 00:10:49,109
CHOWN (change file owners), NET_BIND_SERVICE (listen on ports below 1024),

146
00:10:49,109 --> 00:10:55,987
SYS_ADMIN (mount file systems and much more), SYS_TIME (set the clock) and so on.

147
00:10:55,987 --> 00:11:00,403
Docker gives containers a reduced default set of 14.

148
00:11:00,403 --> 00:11:03,460
Most applications need none of them.

149
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:09,160
