174
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:10,676
I keep hearing about resource limits for security.

175
00:13:10,676 --> 00:13:12,225
What is it, really?

176
00:13:12,767 --> 00:13:18,024
Containers share the host's CPU, memory, process table and open-file table.

177
00:13:18,024 --> 00:13:21,669
Without limits, one container, buggy or compromised,

178
00:13:21,669 --> 00:13:26,857
can exhaust them and take every other container and the host down with it:

179
00:13:26,857 --> 00:13:29,380
a denial of service from the inside.

180
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:33,516
Limits turn "the host is down" into "one container failed".

181
00:13:35,267 --> 00:13:40,213
By default, a container may create as many processes as the host allows:

182
