197
00:15:01,733 --> 00:15:02,447
Got it.

198
00:15:02,447 --> 00:15:05,198
What do I need to remember?

199
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:10,000
Unlimited containers can exhaust the host's processes, memory and CPU:

200
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,708
a denial of service from the inside.

201
00:15:14,267 --> 00:15:22,061
--pids-limit stops fork bombs; --ulimit nofile bounds open files; --memory and --cpus bound the rest.

202
